      "title": "Embracing Digital Transformation",
      "summary": "Embracing Digital Transformation Embracing Digital Home Guidance Briefings (EDTW) What changed Interviews (EDT) How others did it Architectural Deep Dives What to do next Learn Digital Transformation Overview Pillars AI, Cyber, Data, Edge, Computing, Comms ODXA Domains &amp; mappings Whitepapers Monthly canonical synthesis Articles Explainers &amp; analysis Lectures (DTA) Learning series Intelligence Community Community Newsletter Patreon LinkedIn About About Host Sponsors Shop Search Casey Cuny LinkedIn Profile Biography I'm an educator, innovator, and advocate for student-centered learning — named the 2024 California Teacher of the Year and the 2025 Delphi Award winner at National University. As a high school English teacher, instructional coach, and university professor, I bridge the gap between K–12 and higher ed. My passion lies in transforming classrooms through relationship-driven rigor, purposeful use of AI, and equity-focused instructional design. I believe technology should amplify humanity, not replace it — and that the best teaching still feels like mentorship, not management. I’ve developed district-wide trainings on AI in education, created AI-powered writing tutors, and led national conversations on the future of teaching. Whether I’m coaching teachers, guiding student inquiry, or presenting at conferences, my mission is to inspire and empower my students, of all ages, to become lifelong learners, critical thinkers, and ethical leaders. I value innovation, creativity, and excellence in education, and I am always eager to learn new skills and methods to enhance my teaching practice. Latest Episodes Put the title Right Here The real AI literacy challenge isn’t learning the tool — it’s protecting human judgment while using it well. Dr. Darren sits down with Casey Cooney, California Teacher of the Year, to explore how AI in education can deep… Copyright &copy; Paidar Productions LLC All rights reserved",
